Adds the runner half of aarch64 SMT support (PLAN-ARM64-SMT.md). The
Firecracker half is a 4-commit fork rebased onto v1.16.1
(v1.16.1-rlpsmt1): MPIDR_EL1 affinity + a `cpu-map` FDT node, and the
lifting of aarch64's blanket `SmtNotSupported` rejection. Needed for the
NVIDIA Vera runner, whose Olympus CPUs are the fleet's first arm64 parts
with real SMT (2 threads/core, 88 cores x 2 sockets).

Manager.smt comes from RLP_FC_SMT (default off, per-runner A/B like ksm
and balloon) and reaches Firecracker through one helper, m.fcSmt, at all
three fc.Config sites — cold boot, template build, persistent boot.

fcSmt returns nil (field OMITTED, not false) unless BOTH hold:

  * RLP_FC_SMT=1 — the operator asserts an SMT-capable Firecracker is
    installed. This is not cosmetic: models.MachineConfiguration.Smt is
    *bool+omitempty, and upstream FC rejects the field on aarch64 with
    MachineConfigError::SmtNotSupported, so an explicit `smt: false`
    would fail every boot on a stock arm64 runner. Until now the runner
    only ever worked on arm64 because nothing set the field at all — by
    accident, with no test pinning it. TestFirecrackerConfigsUseFcSmtHelper
    now makes that deliberate, in the same source-level style as the
    ForwardSignals guard.

  * an EVEN vcpu count > 1 — every Firecracker rejects smt=true with an
    odd vcpu_count (InvalidVcpuCount), and the fork pairs vCPUs
    (2i, 2i+1) as the two threads of core i, so an odd count has no
    valid pairing. Odd and single-vCPU shapes silently boot without SMT
    instead of failing the create; sizing, capacity and billing are
    untouched.

TemplateKey gains SMT (omitempty) for the same reason Balloon is in the
key: the flag is frozen into the snapshot's machine config at build time
and restored from it, so a clone inherits the template's topology and an
SMT sandbox must never resume a non-SMT template. It records the
EFFECTIVE value — an odd-vCPU template under RLP_FC_SMT=1 boots exactly
as before and keeps its historical hash, which matters because the hash
is both the on-disk dir name and the chunk-CAS content address.

No pause/fullsnap manifest change is needed: smt lives in the snapshot's
own machine config, so a restore cannot disagree with its source. The
existing fc_version gate already separates forked from stock runners.

Signed-off-by: Vedran Jukic <vedran.jukic@gmail.com>
